.SH NAME
.PP
auto-sync-pxe-root-pw - Copy the root password from PXE install image

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-sync-pxe-root-pw
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
None
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-sync-pxe-root-pw
command
syncs the root password in a PXE install image to the
current root account.  This is used to automatically set the
root password following a PXE operating system installation.
The PXE installer image must be in a standard location, as
when created by auto-pxe-installer-setup(8).

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
LOCALBASE/etc/auto-admin/pxe, /etc/master.passwd
.ad
.fi

